Cell["\<\
The gauge direction is {Cos[angle], Sin[angle], 0}. Two- or three-component \
coordinates are accepted; two-component points are padded with zero z.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1125518106,ExpressionUUID->"4b632eff-e8e8-ca4b-8e67-430169258a0e"],

Cell["\<\
The implementation returns Exp[I Pi ((rf-ri).n) (Cross[rf+ri, {0,0,Bz}].n)]. \
The numerical inputs must already use consistent charge, flux, and length \
units; no physical constants are inserted.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->596506455,ExpressionUUID->"a14fc772-87ab-a74d-a4b8-38dc5d116299"],

Cell["\<\
Reversing the two real coordinate arguments conjugates the phase for real Bz \
and angle.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->418907954,ExpressionUUID->"64b4d3fe-8094-b849-b2f0-d15010d111a8"]
}, Closed]],

